3.1 Deﬁnition of the problem
In a typical 3D BPP, a set of items must be packed into ﬁxedsized bins in the way that minimizes the number of bins used. Unlike typical BPP with ﬁxed-sized bins, we focus on the problem of designing the bin with least surface area that could pack all the items. In real business scenarios, such as crossboard e-commerce, no ﬁxed-sized bin is available and ﬂexible and soft materials are used to pack all the items. At the same time, the cost of a bin is directly proportional to its surface area. In this case, minimizing the surface area for the bin would bring great economic beneﬁts.
