B NP-hardness of New Type of 3D BPP
Lemma B.1 The new type of 3D BPP proposed in this paper is NP-hard.
Proof: First of all, we will prove the new type of 2D BPP is NP-hard. To show it is NP-hard, we will give a reduction of 1D Bin Packing Problem.
Given a one-dimensional bin packing problem, it consists of n items with integer size w1, · · · , wn and bins with integer capacity W . The objective is to minimize the number of bins used to pack all items.
To convert it into new type of 2D BPP, we assume that there are n items with width wi and height 1/(n · max(wi)). And there is also a item with width W and height W · n · max(wi), which is called as Base Item. The new type of 2D BPP problem is to ﬁnd the bin with least surface area to pack the generated n + 1 items.
